===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|hǫnd}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*handuz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/hœnt/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|œnt|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|handar|hendur}}

# {{lb|is|anatomy}} [[hand]]
#: ''Mér er illt í '''hendinni'''.''
#:: My '''hand''' hurts.
# {{lb|is|anatomy}} [[arm]]
# [[side]], [[hand]]
#: ''Og ykkur á hægri '''hönd''' sjáið þið Esjuna.''
#:: And on your right '''hand''' you can see the Esja.
# [[hand]], [[handwriting]] (someone's personal style of writing)

====Usage notes====
* The dative form ''hönd'' is used in the sense of “handwriting”.
* A nominative-accusative plural form ''höndur'' exists, but is mostly obsolete.
* The alternative form {{m|is|hendi}} is sometimes used for nominative and accusative singular in [[non-standard]] [[colloquial]] speech; especially regarding sports.

